  "notes": "An ichidan verb. More dynamic and literary than {走|はし}る (to run). Often appears in compound verbs.\n\nCOMMON COMPOUND VERBS:\n- {駆|か}け{上|あ}がる (dash up)\n- {駆|か}け{下|お}りる (dash down)\n- {駆|か}けつける (rush to the scene)\n- {駆|か}け{抜|ぬ}ける (dash through)\n- {駆|か}け{回|まわ}る (run around)\n- {駆|か}け{込|こ}む (rush into)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{走|はし}る is the standard neutral word for running. {駆|か}ける is more vivid and implies speed, urgency, or dynamic motion. {疾走|しっそう}する is even more formal and literary.",
